Subject: [SE4-P1] mfmediaengine retain control intent and buffering events

Residual against GE-Proton11-9 after ge-video-rework.
Source-reviewed only: not compiler or runtime qualification.
Prior P19b2 patch ownership (some behavior is now upstream):
  ge-proton11-6-a320/0007-mf-reprime-and-resume-after-vod-seeks.patch
  ge-proton11-6-a320/0017-winedmo-propagate-terminal-network-read-errors.patch
  ge-proton11-6-a320/0023-mfmediaengine-check-seekability-before-recovery-reset.patch
  ge-proton11-6/0004-winedmo-async-http-and-repair-vod-seeking.patch
  ge-proton11-6/0006-winedmo-recover-interrupted-vod-seeks.patch
  ge-proton11-6/0013-mfmediaengine-reconcile-pause-scrub-intent.patch
  ge-proton11-6/0014-mfmediaengine-preserve-pending-start-position.patch
  ge-proton11-6/0020-quiet-ge-media-diagnostics.patch
  ge-proton11-7-se2-p19b/0039-mf-report-terminal-direct-filter-errors.patch
  ge-proton11-7-se2-p19b/0077-mf-mfmediaengine-consume-buffering-events.patch
  proposed/0034-mfmediaengine-honor-ready-source-autoplay.patch
  proposed/0036-mfmediaengine-guard-audio-only-segment-end.patch
  proposed/0040-mfmediaengine-remove-uninitialized-topology-cleanup.patch
  proposed/0055-mfmediaengine-wait-for-renderer-drain-before-ended.patch
  proposed/0058-mfmediaengine-share-immediate-seek-policy.patch

SE4-P1: rebased onto GE-Proton11-12's ge-video-rework 0104, which sends no
WAITING from Play() for a live source. Buffering always raises
BUFFERINGSTARTED and BUFFERINGENDED; WAITING and PLAYING follow them only for
a source that is not live. The engine still enters and leaves its waiting
state for a live source, so a Play() during a stall does not restart it.

